  body: "# Evidence for DMG overpayment recoverability\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe overpayment chapter
    places the initial recoverability burden on the decision maker and calls for further enquiries when evidence
    is insufficient, including evidence that entitlement decisions were changed.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\n\
    Missing records are not proof of their contents. The appeal material may need the warnings and instructions
    actually issued; the source permits explained nearest equivalents where the original print is unavailable. No
    claimant-specific conclusion is modelled.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 09175, PDF page 38](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/678776493a9388161c5d23d5/dmgch09.pdf#page=38)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 9: Overpayments, offsets and recoverability.\n- [DMG 09176, PDF page 38](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/678776493a9388161c5d23d5/dmgch09.pdf#page=38)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 9: Overpayments, offsets and recoverability.\n- [DMG 09027, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/678776493a9388161c5d23d5/dmgch09.pdf#page=5)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 9: Overpayments, offsets and recoverability.\n- [DMG 09180, PDF page 39](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/678776493a9388161c5d23d5/dmgch09.pdf#page=39)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 9: Overpayments, offsets and recoverability.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch9` PDF SHA-256: `96933fc64fcacb0a3e253a686218757a85fb415574fde11e4d3435149b1a2505`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `069cefdb6e8a7486021d251c6991ef627fc063a3b842eff2e98cde688ed831d2`.\n- `dmg-vol1-ch6`
    PDF SHA-256: `dcd2a7ede4499792d9bc6762c94a2d6c0ca6e811cb077abbbd4e41e4d405a4e4`; extracted pages SHA-256: `e95434f7e856adbd1c8550b369066644a6bf6aa7567af05a1d41768d3dae0c3e`.\n\
    \nThe publicly acquired chapter 6 PDF carries the printed footer “Official - DWP Use Only”. This observation
    is preserved alongside its public acquisition URL; the source owner should clarify any conflict with intended
    reuse. It is not evidence of access to unpublished material.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-burden-of-proof
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter expressly allocates the initial recoverability burden to the DM.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch9/0038
      quote: "09175 The onus of proof that overpaid benefit is recoverable initially rests with the DM 1.\n\n\n\
        \                                                                                       1 SS A Act 92, s
        71(1)"
      locator: DMG 09175
  - target: term/dmg-overpayment-recoverability
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source links sufficiency of evidence to deciding both the overpayment and recoverability
      questions.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch9/0038
      quote: "09176 The DM should\n\n\n1. examine the evidence and decide whether it is sufficient to determine
        the overpayment and the\n\nrecoverability question1 and\n\n\n2. make further enquiries where evidence is
        insufficient and\n\n\n3. bear in mind that if statements made by the DM are contested at any appeal hearing,
        the FtT will look\n\nfor supporting evidence2.\n\n\n                                                   \
        \                       1 SS A Act 92, s 71; 2 R(SB) 10/86"
      locator: DMG 09176
  - target: term/dmg-tribunal-evidence-disclosure
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The appeals chapter gives specific warnings-and-instructions evidence for a
      recoverable-overpayment appeal.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch6/0048
      quote: "06306 If an appeal is made against a recoverable overpayment, the evidence should include\n\n\n1.
        the warnings and instructions in a printed form\n\n\n2. a copy of any leaflet sent to the claimant if the
        advice in that leaflet is relevant.\n\n\nIf the particular print of a form or leaflet is no longer available,
        the nearest equivalent should be included.\nIf there have been any changes to the warnings and instructions
        to the claimant then the DM should\ninclude an explanation as to the effect, if any, those changes have
        on the case."
      locator: DMG 06306
